{"id":"s1.3.9","slug":"a-x-a-b-trick","title":"a x a/b Trick","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">When multiplying an integer $a$ by a fraction of the form $\\frac{a}{b}$, you can use the formula:</p><p class=\"text-center font-bold mb-4\">$a \\times \\frac{a}{b} = [a + (a - b)] + \\frac{(a - b)^2}{b}$</p><p class=\"mb-4\">If the fraction is less than 1, you subtract the difference $(a-b)$ from $a$. If the fraction is greater than 1, you add it.</p><p>For $11 \\times \\frac{11}{13}$: $a=11, b=13, a-b=-2$. The result is $[11 + (-2)] + \\frac{(-2)^2}{13} = 9\\frac{4}{13}$.</p><p>For $13 \\times \\frac{13}{12}$: $a=13, b=12, a-b=1$. The result is $[13 + 1] + \\frac{1^2}{12} = 14\\frac{1}{12}$.</p><p>Sometimes it is simpler to just convert to an improper fraction and solve directly.</p>","summary":"When multiplying an integer by a fraction of the form , you can use the formula: If the fraction is less than 1, you subtract the difference from .","generation_guideline":"Generate a problem of the form a * (a/b).","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Calculate $11 \\times \\frac{11}{14}$. (mixed number)","answer":"8 9/14","kind":"exact","requiredForm":"mixed","tags":["arithmetic","fractions"]},{"id":2,"text":"Calculate $22 \\times \\frac{22}{25}$. (mixed number)","answer":"19 9/25","kind":"exact","requiredForm":"mixed","tags":["arithmetic","fractions"]},{"id":3,"text":"Calculate $19 \\times \\frac{19}{23}$. (mixed number)","answer":"15 16/23","kind":"exact","requiredForm":"mixed","tags":["arithmetic","fractions"]},{"id":4,"text":"Calculate $27 \\times \\frac{27}{32}$. (mixed number)","answer":"22 25/32","kind":"exact","requiredForm":"mixed","tags":["arithmetic","fractions"]},{"id":5,"text":"Calculate $16 \\times \\frac{16}{19}$. (mixed number)","answer":"13 9/19","kind":"exact","requiredForm":"mixed","tags":["arithmetic","fractions"]},{"id":6,"text":"Calculate $29 \\times \\frac{29}{34}$. (mixed number)","answer":"24 25/34","kind":"exact","requiredForm":"mixed","tags":["arithmetic","fract